WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.750
(dramatic music)

00:00:15.810 --> 00:00:18.810
- [Narrator] If you have
benign prostatic hyperplasia

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:22.880
or BPH, your prostate gland is enlarged.

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:26.890
The prostate is a
walnut-sized gland in men.

00:00:26.890 --> 00:00:28.460
Just beneath your bladder,

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:31.490
your prostate gland
surrounds your urethra,

00:00:31.490 --> 00:00:35.850
the tube through which urine
and semen exit your body.

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:39.100
Your seminal vesicles
and prostate make fluid

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:42.353
that combines with sperm
cells to create semen.

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:49.040
During normal urination,
urine flows from your bladder

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:51.910
through the part of your
urethra inside your prostate,

00:00:51.910 --> 00:00:54.973
then through the rest of your
urethra to leave your body.

00:00:57.470 --> 00:00:58.920
For unknown reasons,

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:02.173
your prostate gland may
enlarge as you get older.

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:06.620
If you have benign prostatic hyperplasia,

00:01:06.620 --> 00:01:09.150
your prostate may grow
large enough to narrow

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:12.323
or block the part of your
urethra that runs through it.

00:01:13.370 --> 00:01:16.390
As a result, your
enlarged prostate may slow

00:01:16.390 --> 00:01:19.763
or block the urine flow out
of your body when you urinate.

00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:26.610
The symptoms of benign
prostatic hyperplasia include

00:01:26.610 --> 00:01:31.610
frequent urination or urge to
urinate, especially at night,

00:01:31.710 --> 00:01:34.690
a weak or interrupted urine stream,

00:01:34.690 --> 00:01:36.473
and straining to urinate.

00:01:38.950 --> 00:01:42.830
Over time, untreated benign
prostatic hyperplasia

00:01:42.830 --> 00:01:47.830
may cause the following
complications: inability to urinate,

00:01:47.930 --> 00:01:52.740
damage to your bladder and
kidneys, bladder infections,

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:57.463
bladder stones, and urine
leakage, called incontinence.

00:02:01.750 --> 00:02:04.250
If you have benign prostatic hyperplasia

00:02:04.250 --> 00:02:06.190
with mild or no symptoms,

00:02:06.190 --> 00:02:08.850
your doctor may recommend
watchful waiting,

00:02:08.850 --> 00:02:11.850
which includes getting your
prostate checked every year

00:02:11.850 --> 00:02:15.413
to make sure your symptoms or
health are not getting worse.

00:02:16.490 --> 00:02:19.170
If you have moderate
symptoms that bother you,

00:02:19.170 --> 00:02:21.480
your doctor may recommend medication,

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:23.760
such as alpha-blockers.

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:26.040
Alpha-blockers relax muscle tissue

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:28.540
in the neck of your
bladder and in the urethra

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:30.363
to improve your urine flow.

00:02:32.150 --> 00:02:35.980
5 alpha reductase inhibitors
may also improve urine flow

00:02:35.980 --> 00:02:39.783
over several months by reducing
the size of your prostate.

00:02:41.960 --> 00:02:44.110
You may receive a combination therapy

00:02:44.110 --> 00:02:45.973
of both types of drugs.

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:51.550
If medication isn't
relieving your symptoms,

00:02:51.550 --> 00:02:54.240
your doctor may recommend
a surgical procedure

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:59.000
called transurethral resection
of the prostate or TURP.

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:00.450
During this procedure,

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:03.820
your surgeon will insert an
instrument called a cystoscope

00:03:03.820 --> 00:03:06.593
through your urethra
to reach your prostate.

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:12.410
Then a wire tool called a
resectoscope will be inserted

00:03:12.410 --> 00:03:15.070
through the cystoscope
to shave off tissue,

00:03:15.070 --> 00:03:17.073
which will widen your urethra.

00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:20.250
Other minimally invasive variations

00:03:20.250 --> 00:03:23.340
on this type of procedure use lasers,

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:27.040
microwaves, radio waves,
or electrical energy

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:29.470
from tools inserted through the cystoscope

00:03:29.470 --> 00:03:32.483
to remove some or all
of your prostate gland.

00:03:34.410 --> 00:03:36.660
If your prostate is very large,

00:03:36.660 --> 00:03:40.303
your doctor may recommend an
open prostatectomy procedure.

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:43.300
In open prostatectomy,

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:46.313
your surgeon will make an
incision in your lower abdomen.

00:03:47.790 --> 00:03:49.800
After exposing your prostate,

00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:53.183
your surgeon will make an
incision in its outer capsule.

00:03:55.510 --> 00:03:58.793
Next, the tissue inside your
prostate will be removed,

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:03.023
and the capsule incision
will be closed with sutures.

00:04:05.230 --> 00:04:07.710
Finally, your skin incision will be closed

00:04:07.710 --> 00:04:09.473
with sutures or staples.

00:04:12.730 --> 00:04:15.770
You can't prevent benign
prosthetic hyperplasia,

00:04:15.770 --> 00:04:17.700
but the following lifestyle changes

00:04:17.700 --> 00:04:20.130
can make your symptoms less severe.

00:04:20.130 --> 00:04:23.830
Avoid medication that can make
it harder for you to urinate,

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:27.420
such as antihistamines and decongestants.

00:04:27.420 --> 00:04:31.320
Stop drinking fluids for a
few hours before bedtime.

00:04:31.320 --> 00:04:35.640
Avoid drinking alcohol or
fluids that contain caffeine.

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:38.530
Try to empty your bladder
by double voiding.

00:04:38.530 --> 00:04:41.660
To double void, urinate,
wait a few minutes,

00:04:41.660 --> 00:04:43.853
and then try to urinate again.

